  "title": "Multi-agent automated code review",
  "description": "## Multi-agent automated code review\n\nA left-to-right lifecycle across the top row: pull-request intake resolves and gates the change, context assembly ranks source material, specialist reviewers run in parallel, and aggregation validates findings before publication. The bottom row shows publication policy, human feedback and threshold calibration, head-change cancellation/restart, and telemetry-driven budget degradation.\n\nSolid teal/green/orange edges carry the primary review and feedback flow. Dashed edges show lifecycle controls: calibrated thresholds feed future validation, head changes cancel and restart intake, and exhausted daily budgets restrict later runs to correctness and security reviewers.",
